  "semantics": {
    "session": "Owner is MSP descriptor plus nonzero session token. Token is not authentication.",
    "open": "Request token=0, requestId nonzero, nonce nonzero. Identical owner/nonce/target/backend/requestId OPEN retries return current same session. Other OPEN returns BUSY. OPEN receipt is terminal only after READY or failure.",
    "ordering": "GET/SET/SAVE/CLOSE IDs strictly increase with no wrap in session. Last identical request returns current cached result; same ID with different payload INVALID_REQUEST; lower ID STALE_REQUEST. STATUS ID0 reads last result; nonzero must match last accepted ID.",
    "poll": "STATUS updates only owner heartbeat, not result/request identity. BUSY while operation pending, terminal bit clear. Completion retained until next accepted request or close.",
    "close": "CLOSE may abort pending operation. release does not claim ESC restart. If transport entered and not positively recovered, POWER_CYCLE_NEEDED/RESTART_REQUIRED remains and arming inhibit retained. Closed session retries are retained until next OPEN; STATUS can observe retained close result.",
    "defaults": "No adapter means CAPS backend0 capabilities1 validatedTargets0 flags17; OPEN unsupported without pin changes.",
    "save": "SET is volatile RAM + readback. SAVE OK means CLI completion, not power-cycle persistence. Unknown write outcomes are distinct and cannot auto-retry save.",
    "limits": "Fixed32 replies, maximum14 requests, owner timeout10000ms, CLI transaction timeout2000ms; tests and clients poll while busy.",
    "identity": "Schema1 supports exactly ESCape32 revision17 patch2 or patch3. CLI CFG_MAP and checkcfg are byte-identical between pinned17.2 and17.3 sources. Unknown revisions, including17.4 and16.3, expose identity-only schema0 and reject GET/SET/SAVE. No arbitrary CLI or BEC/mode/reset/throttle operations."
  },
